    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317218": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator University, Provost Office",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator University, Provost Office - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Administrative Coordinator University, Provost Office ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500601230821 Posted Date 8/26/2026 Salary Grade Grade 46 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $24.00 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $27.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Reporting to the Director of Academic Program Review (APR), with work assigned by the Assistant Provost for Operations, the Administrative Coordinator (AC) for Academic Initiatives & Operational Excellence is an important member of the Office of the Provost and supports both APR as well as general office operations. Must be able to work independently, anticipate office needs, manage work across varying projects, set priorities in consultation with others, and handle sensitive/confidential information. Work focuses mainly on administrative support for APR, including event planning and management, as well as coverage of the reception desk on a daily basis. This role is 100% in-person, with no hybrid option. Scheduled work hours are Monday-Friday, 8:30-5:00 at 1 Silber Way, 8th Floor. Occasional evening hours may be required, as determined by the supervisor, during peak periods of operation. Required Skills Bachelor's degree and 1-3 years of experience is required. Experience may be substituted for education in certain circumstances. Excellent communication and organizational skills, including ability to write well and to deal effectively and diplomatically with various constituencies. Careful attention to detail is necessary. Familiarity with Microsoft Office Suite, WordPress, and SharePoint is desired. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located at 1 Silber Way, \r\nExecutive Administration Center, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317032": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator, BU Residence Life",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator, BU Residence Life - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Administrative Coordinator, BU Residence Life ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500395720713 Posted Date 7/16/2026 Salary Grade Grade 24 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $2,091.00 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $2,808.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Administrative Coordinator provides administrative and operational support to the Associate Director of Residence Life for Operations and the graduate residence life operation. This role assists with a range of operational projects, data management, and reporting, as well as managing the day-to-day functions of the graduate residence life operation, including move-in and move-out coordination and key distribution. The Administrative Coordinator serves as a key point of contact for students, University colleagues, and external partners, ensuring efficient and professional office operations. Required Skills High School Diploma, B.A./B.S. preferred, strong administrative skills and one to three years of related experience. MUST INCLUDE COVER LETTER IN ORDER TO BE CONSIDERED. This position is 9.7 months We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located at 25 Buick St, \r\nAdministrative Offices, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317145": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator, ODEM School of Social Work",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator, ODEM School of Social Work - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Administrative Coordinator, ODEM School of Social Work ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500131560727 Posted Date 8/10/2026 Salary Grade Grade 26 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $23.67 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $26.92 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Boston University School of Social Work (BUSSW) is seeking a highly organized and detail-oriented Administrative Coordinator to join the Office of Data and Enrollment Management (ODEM). This position is a vital member of the team, providing essential administrative support to students, alumni, faculty, and staff. Reporting to the Director of Data and Enrollment Management, the Administrative Coordinator will: Respond promptly and professionally to a high volume of email inquiries. Assist with the auditing and maintenance of student records to ensure accuracy and compliance. Process student and alumni verification requests. Support the School's data reporting and analysis needs. Coordinate key operational processes for incoming students and graduation activities. Maintain and update the ODEM website, creating online forms to ensure information is accurate and accessible. Required Skills Associate's degree or equivalent work experience. Minimum of 1–3 years of administrative experience, preferably in an academic or customer service environment. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite; experience with database systems and website content management tools preferred. Preferred Skills: Experience in higher education administration. Knowledge of student information systems and academic record-keeping. Why Join Us: Boston University offers a competitive salary, generous benefits, and the opportunity to be part of a mission-driven institution that values diversity, equity, and inclusion. BUSSW is nationally recognized for its commitment to social justice and preparing graduates to make meaningful contributions in their communities. To Apply Submit your application, including a cover letter and resume. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located at 264 Bay State Rd, \r\nSchool of Social Work, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317135": {
      "title": "Animal Care Technician Lab, Animal Care Facility",
      "description": "Animal Care Technician Lab, Animal Care Facility - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Animal Care Technician Lab, Animal Care Facility ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500044800804 Posted Date 8/7/2026 Salary Grade Grade 24 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $21.00 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $22.50 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Animal Science Center is part of the Office of Research, a group dedicated to aiding the research community in navigating the lifecycle of their work, from finding funding to creating proposals to helping inventions find their way to the public. We are a diverse group of passionate, enthusiastic personnel who understand and appreciate the importance research animals are to furthering scientific discoveries. Our mission is to ensure while aiding in academic studies, that animal care, health and welfare is maintained at the highest standards according to Institutional, local, state, and federal regulations, policies and procedures. To accomplish this goal, this candidate would complete daily quality animal care for all housed research animals such as rats, mice, birds, on the Charles River Campus. The candidate's assignments would include animal husbandry tasks such as cage changing, animal health checks, veterinary health monitoring and treatment, and facility maintenance. Additional responsibilities include: Animal receiving and housing, census data collection, and others as assigned. Training would include following standard operating procedures for Biosafety Levels: ASBL-1 and ASBL-2 and Chemical Containment Levels: CCL-1, CCL-2 and CCL3. Animal Science Center is looking for a candidate who is ready to work in a dynamic, positive work environment surround by likeminded individuals. Someone who can complete assignments independently and as a whole. An ideal candidate would be eager to learn and can effectively communicate via email, text, call, through smartphone and computers. Skills such as accurate record keeping and being detail oriented would be desirable for this position. This candidate would be professional and courteous, while building working relationships with researchers, veterinary staff, and co-workers. This is a union represented position. Why work at BU? Animal Science Center is committed to your professional development and providing opportunities for you to pursue your professional goals. Boston University's benefit package includes health, dental, life insurance, and paid time off. Full-time employees are also eligible for tuition remission for courses at Boston University. Noteworthy: the remission benefit extends to dependents as well. Required Skills High school diploma or GED required. Previous experience preferred but not required. This position is 40 hours per week. Schedule is Tuesday to Saturday. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located at 590 Commonwealth Ave, \r\nMetcalf Science Center, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317065": {
      "title": "Instruction Assistant, Special Collections, Research Services",
      "description": "Instruction Assistant, Special Collections, Research Services - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Instruction Assistant, Special Collections, Research Services ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26501024160720 Posted Date 7/24/2026 Salary Grade Grade 25 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $21.63 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $25.51 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Boston University Libraries seek an Archives Instruction Assistant for a 3-year grant-funded instruction program in the Howard Gotlieb Archival Research Center within Boston University Libraries. This position’s responsibilities include assisting Research and Instruction Archivists with planning, preparation, and hosting undergraduate class visits to the archives. It also includes providing day-of support (during Registrar scheduled class times which can be outside of the centers operational hours which are 8-5) for instruction sessions with faculty, including moving and tracking material to and from collection storage. Additionally, this position provides research support by seeking examples of material in collections that might be useful to highlight in a teaching and learning context, helping faculty build class assignments, and light collection description to aid research. A successful candidate will also work with Instruction Archivists to support the creation of Learning Resources Repository objects for future classroom use. The grant is focused on increasing undergraduate student engagement with the archives of select civil and human rights leaders at BU. Reporting to the Research and Instruction Archives, the assistant will be a key collaborator supporting the archival instruction program and research initiatives. The incumbant will manage the logistics of class visits, including coordinating with archivists on bookings, scheduling, collections requests, and room setup, while helping faculty and students navigate our collections and reading room policies. Responsibilities include assisting with instruction assessment, tracking class visits and trends to inform program development. Occasional evening and weekend availability may be required. Beyond classroom support, the assistant will work closely with graduate research assistants, faculty, and our research and instruction teams to identify collection materials that align with course objectives. Using finding aids and research guides, the assistant will identify relevant materials and maintain topical resource lists for future classes. The role contributes to creating engaging learning objects, including worksheets, videos, tutorials, and other instructional materials and ensure these tools are discoverable across our course management systems, website, and other platforms. This role offers an excellent opportunity to support student learning and faculty research while deepening your knowledge of archival work. Required Skills Bachelor’s degree. One to three years of relevant experience. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. This is a grant-funded 3-year position. For consideration, please submit a cover letter, CV, and list of professional references. The position will remain open until filled. Working at Boston University Libraries Boston University Libraries is a learning organization that supports BU librarians, archivists, and information and subject specialists seeking and sharing knowledge, practices, and perspectives that advance library collections services, and their own professional development. In a collaborative, supportive, and engaging work environment, BU Libraries expert staff assist multidisciplinary research and exploration, build distinctive collections and archives of enduring research value, and empower users to thrive amid an ever-changing information environment. Located in the heart of Boston, the BU Libraries are embedded in numerous vibrant regional and national library and information specialist networks. The BU Libraries are active members within the Boston Library Consortium (BLC), the Association of Research Libraries (ARL), the Northeast Research Libraries Consortium (NERL), HathiTrust, and the Coalition for Networked Information (CNI), and library staff at BU serve as engaged thought-leaders on a wide breadth of library management and service areas across diverse communities. Boston University, a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), is one of the leading private research and teaching institutions in the world, with three primary campuses in the heart of Boston and programs around the globe. Chartered in 1869, the University is home to more than 33,000 students from more than 130 countries, 375,000 living alumni, 10,000 faculty and staff, and 17 schools and colleges. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located at 771 Commonwealth Ave, \r\nMugar Library, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/315966": {
      "title": "Position Type",
      "description": "MACHINIST, SENIOR, EXPERIMENTAL, College of Arts & Sciences, Physics - BOSTON, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply MACHINIST, SENIOR, EXPERIMENTAL, College of Arts & Sciences, Physics ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location BOSTON, MA, United States Tracking Code 25500253441002 Posted Date 10/2/2025 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $32.00 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $38.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Established in 1873, Arts and Sciences is Boston University's largest and most academically diverse unit, encompassing over 8,400 undergraduates, 2,000 graduate students, 800 faculty members, and 300 staff across 50 departments, programs, centers, and institutes. Our faculty are award-winning researchers, innovative teachers, and dedicated mentors committed to exploring the complexities of our present and past, uncovering new perspectives, and crafting creative solutions to real-world problems. Our staff are dynamic, mission-driven professionals who foster community, inclusion, and belonging to advance every aspect of the college enterprise. Our community thrives on collaboration, bold ideas, and interdisciplinary exploration. Join us in supporting the pursuit of knowledge that changes the world and provides boundless opportunities to inspire the next generation of leaders. We offer generous benefits, including health, dental, and life insurance, tuition remission, retirement savings, paid time off, and holiday leave. The Senior Experimental Machinist Perform highly skilled precision work in the design, development, machining, fabrication, assembly, and testing of a wide variety of scientific instruments and experimental equipment. Interact with scientists, engineers and students as required by supervisor on issues related to these tasks. Collaborate with a team of co-workers in a state-of-the- art facility. Requires: Vocational/technical training, excellent knowledge of Computer Numeric Control (CNC) and conventional machining techniques, CNC programming in Mastercam and a plus if knows SolidWorks for design, tooling equipment and machining standards, and a five to eight years of experience minimum. Required Skills Vocational/technical training, excellent knowledge of Computer Numeric Control (CNC) and conventional machining techniques, CNC programming in Mastercam and a plus if knows SolidWorks for design, tooling equipment and machining standards. Five to eight years of experience minimum. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located in BOSTON, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317017": {
      "title": "OFFICE COORDINATOR, College of Arts & Sciences, Biology",
      "description": "OFFICE COORDINATOR, College of Arts & Sciences, Biology - BOSTON, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply OFFICE COORDINATOR, College of Arts & Sciences, Biology ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location BOSTON, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500099770711 Posted Date 7/13/2026 Salary Grade Grade 25 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $21.63 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $23.50 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Established in 1873, Arts and Sciences is Boston University's largest and most academically diverse unit, encompassing over 8,400 undergraduates, 2,000 graduate students, 800 faculty members, and 300 staff across 50 departments, programs, centers, and institutes. Our faculty are award-winning researchers, innovative teachers, and dedicated mentors committed to exploring the complexities of our present and past, uncovering new perspectives, and crafting creative solutions to real-world problems. Our staff are dynamic, mission-driven professionals who foster community, inclusion, and belonging to advance every aspect of the college enterprise. Our community thrives on collaboration, bold ideas, and interdisciplinary exploration. Join us in supporting the pursuit of knowledge that changes the world and provides boundless opportunities to inspire the next generation of leaders. We offer generous benefits, including health, dental, and life insurance, tuition remission, retirement savings, paid time off, and holiday leave. Boston University's Department of Biology seeks an Office Coordinator to act as the primary and first point of contact for visitors to its main administrative office. There are two overarching components to this position: Handling inquiries, including phone calls, emails, web submissions to the Biology Department main office according to department priorities and protocol. Providing administrative support for Biology's large teaching and research operations particularly its undergraduate program. The incumbent will assist visitors with inquiries, provide administrative support by either directly addressing or directing those to other Biology staff, faculty and/or central units. Other responsibilities include: Ordering supplies sorting mail, scheduling room reservations, and conducting initial student screenings during advising. They will also assist with departmental events and department deliveries, as well as maintaining departmental databases. This role involves supervising Work Study students, ensuring that operational procedures and basic etiquette are followed, and accurate information is disseminated to dept stakeholders. Act as primary contact point for all visitors, incoming phone calls, emails, website submissions, and students and faculty to the Biology Department main office. Filter and disseminate materials and information in a timely manner to the appropriate destination point in a professional manner. Prepare and maintain department information lists for interdepartmental use. Ensure smooth operation of front desk. Required Skills A cover letter is required for consideration. Associate's degree required, 1-3 years of relevant work experience. The ideal candidate will possess good interpersonal, written and oral communication skills and must be able to function independently, prioritize work with tact and discretion. The ability to follow-up until issues are resolved and tasks are completed across broad and varying activity is a critical skill for this position. The biology department is a large, collaborative and dynamic environment that values diversity and inclusion. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located in BOSTON, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/316382": {
      "title": "PROGRAM COORDINATOR, RESIDENCE SERVICES, AUXILARY, Office of Housing",
      "description": "PROGRAM COORDINATOR, RESIDENCE SERVICES, AUXILARY, Office of Housing - BOSTON, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply PROGRAM COORDINATOR, RESIDENCE SERVICES, AUXILARY, Office of Housing ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location BOSTON, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500049840213 Posted Date 2/13/2026 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $21.63 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $21.63 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Provide general office, clerical, and onsite support for the Residence Services operations. Assist with the central key inventory for residential system; conduct key-board inventories at the residence halls. Field a high volume of phone calls and email inquiries from students, parents, and other University departments and provide excellent customer service. Assist in mitigating student room issues out in the field. This position is also responsible for managing vending services, this is the distribution of MicroFridges and Safes during the academic year and summer. Must have ability to lift and carry 50 lbs. •Resolve student and parent complaints with furniture, appliances, and facilities by visiting rooms across campuses especially during move-in/out and transition periods. Coordinate with Facilities Management to resolve any issues with room condition. Monitor and process work orders received through the Maintenance module in StarRez. Organize furniture request, and appliance repairs forms for warehouse staff, and outside vendors. Maintain accurate records and logs of same. •Oversee and conduct damage billing with student staff. At the end of each semester visit empty rooms to inspect overall condition of rooms/suites/apartments. Ensure that appropriate documentation and photographs are collected so that if students appeal, documentation can be provided. Communicate with students and parents about damage and key/lock charges posted to students' accounts. Post charges to student accounts for lost keys, lock changes, and dorm damages. Assist in the Room Condition Report process management and use the data when processing damage billing at the end of each semester. •Monitor move-in and move-out progress in the residences. Monitor accurate placement and retrieval of moving carts, assist students with issues while moving in/out, provide support for the Associate Director with following up on student and parent issues. Monitor and respond to emails in the Housing Residence Services central mailbox. Ensure notes are updated in StarRez. •Process lock change requests, prioritize orders, and coordinate with residence staff on all matters related to issuance and replacement of room keys, missing keys, and lock changes. Conduct key-board inventories and turnovers in the residence hall offices and troubleshoot key issues. •Assist in managing all Vending services operations. This includes the distribution of MicroFridges/Safes, TVs during the academic year and summer, including managing laundry facilities in residential buildings, and UPS storage program. This will also include being responsible for managing the vending service account and responding to emails, calls, website, and budget. •Use FacilityOS software to log and maintain inventory. Coordinate barcoding of furniture and appliances in the residences. Required Skills High School Diploma/GED, B.A./B.S. preferred, and one to three years of experience. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located in BOSTON, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317069": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, Student Academic Life",
      "description": "Program Coordinator, Student Academic Life - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Program Coordinator, Student Academic Life ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500017650723 Posted Date 7/27/2026 Salary Grade Grade 26 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $21.63 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $24.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Administrative Coordinator, Student Academic Services Are you someone who enjoys helping others, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and takes pride in delivering outstanding customer service? Join our Student Academic Services team and play a vital role in supporting students throughout their academic journey. As the first point of contact for our busy advising office, you'll welcome students, faculty, staff, parents, and University partners while providing exceptional administrative and operational support. This role is ideal for someone who is highly organized, detail-oriented, and enjoys balancing customer service with complex administrative responsibilities. What You'll Do: Serve as the primary point of contact for a high-volume undergraduate advising office, providing courteous, accurate, and timely assistance to students, faculty, staff, parents, and University partners. Coordinate appointments and correspondence for academic leadership, advisors, and graduation officers while managing daily front desk operations. Process and maintain a variety of student academic records, including transfer credit evaluations, graduation applications, major and minor declarations, petitions, AP credit, and other academic transactions. Manage office workflows and ensure the accurate processing of student information across multiple University systems. Coordinate special projects, including orientation support, academic communications, publications, and initiatives that support student success. Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise student employees to support the daily operations of the office. Respond thoughtfully to sensitive and time-sensitive student situations, triaging concerns and connecting individuals with the appropriate campus resources. What We're Looking For: Associate's degree required; bachelor's degree preferred. One to three years of administrative, customer service, or higher education experience. Outstanding customer service and interpersonal skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, parents, and University leadership. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated professionalism, sound judgment, and discretion when handling confidential information and sensitive student matters. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and the ability to learn and navigate multiple University systems. Why Join Our Team? This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the student experience while working in a collaborative, student-centered environment. Every day brings new opportunities to solve problems, support student success, and contribute to the mission of the College through excellent service and teamwork. Required Skills Two years of college or equivalent, bachelor's preferred, a high degree of professionalism, strong customer service and communication skills, and one to three years of experience. This position is 35 hours per week. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. In accordance with the Local 2324 collective bargaining agreement, this job will be open to internal applicants only for the first week of posting. Current L2324 represented employees, click here for information on how to apply for this position . This position is located at 100 Bay State Rd, \r\nYawkey Center for Student Services, \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/External/jobs/317251": {
      "title": "OSGP Senior Clinical Coordinator, Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery",
      "description": "OSGP Senior Clinical Coordinator, Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery - Boston, MA, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Home Jobs My Account Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply OSGP Senior Clinical Coordinator, Department of Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Administrative/Support/Clerical Job Location Boston, MA, United States Tracking Code 26500482190901 Posted Date 9/3/2026 Salary Grade Grade 46 Expected Hiring Range Minimum $23.13 Expected Hiring Range Maximum $36.97 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Patient Services: Scheduling appointments, follow-up appointments, and surgery per departmental protocol Verifying patient eligibility and benefits with patient's insurance company Obtaining appropriate HMO primary care physician referrals Registering patients in EPIC at the time of the appointment Administrative: Interacting with students and residents concerning patient care and meetings Answering and transferring telephone calls Screening phone calls: taking detailed messages or sending to voicemail Confirming and delivering facsimiles Pulling patients' charts for daily schedule Preparing clinicians' daily schedule Printing dictation Filing patient information/charts Maintaining patient records in a neat and orderly fashion Recording and tracking archival patient records in database Creating and/or verifying a record for the patient file Contacting doctor's offices to gather patient information and referrals Discussing and collecting fees Writing receipts of patient payment and third party payments Posting accurate visit charges Demonstrating knowledge of medical and dental insurance policies Escorting patients to seating in clinic exam rooms as necessary Problem-solving and multi-tasking to handle multiple patient needs simultaneously Checking availability of assistants for procedures; requests for special equipment arranged; preventing overbooking of appointments; ensuring that all financial considerations are arranged prior to appointment; Required Skills Strong organizational and planning skills required Previous healthcare experience desired We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located at 635 Albany St, \r\nGoldman (G Bldg), \r\nBoston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply Life @ BU Benefits Compensation | Human Resources Faculty and Staff Assistance Office Children's Center Life @ BU Flexible Work Boston University About BU Strategic Plan Community and Inclusion Sustainability Campus Locations Locations Schools and Colleges Questions or Issues? Recruitment Inquiry General HR Inquiry close"
    },
    "https://www.bu.edu/fsao/": {
      "title": "Welcome",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff Assistance Office <![endif]--> Skip to Main Content Faculty & Staff Assistance Office Menu Search Home Services Counseling Mental Health & Well-being Checkups Management Consultation Critical Incidents Workshops & Groups Current Programs Video Library Resources OurRelationship Headspace Mental Well-being Self-Assessments BIPOC Mental Health Trauma Intimate Partner Violence LGBTQIA2S+ Mental Health Apps Self-Care Tips and Resources Manager’s Role with Distressing Current Events Coping with the Current Moment Substance Use and Addictions BU Resources About FSAO FAQs Meet Our Staff FSAO Confidentiality Statement FSAO Diversity Statement Contact Us Crisis Resources Feedback Search Search for: Welcome The Faculty & Staff Assistance Office (FSAO) is a resource where BU faculty and staff can find help for a range of personal, work-related, and family concerns.  Our licensed professionals offer: Free and confidential short-term counseling Referrals for mental health and substance use treatment Referrals to community resources Crisis support (critical incident response) Management consultation Training and education Resources to promote well-being FSAO services are available to all BU employees and their household family members.  Services are offered in person on the Charles River and Medical campuses as well as by phone and virtually. Interpreter services are available . If you have questions about our services or would like to schedule an appointment, please contact us via our Contact Form or by phone at 617-353-5381. Our office is open Monday through Friday between 9:00 am and 5:00 pm.  If you need assistance outside of those hours, please call 911 or one of these Crisis Resources . loading slideshow... 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 Related to From the FSAO September is Suicide Prevention Month August 26, 2026 Suicide Prevention and Support Resources\r\nTips for Accessing Resources:\r\n\r\nAll crisis lines are free... Faculty Resource Fair – 8-26-26 August 21, 2026 Faculty Resource Fair\r\nWednesday, August 26, 11am to 1pm\r\n\r\nDuan Center for Data and... Disability Pride Month is Celebrated in July June 29, 2026 Disability Pride Month is Celebrated in July\r\n\r\nThe FSAO is proud to amplify the message of... Retirement Resources 2026 March 31, 2026 As part of the Spring 2026 HR Pre-Retirement Planning Webinar Series, here... More about Faculty & Staff Assistance Office Locations Charles River Campus 888 Commonwealth Ave, Suite 309 Boston, MA 02215 617-353-5381 Medical Campus 85 E. Newton Street, 818b Boston, MA 02118 617-353-5381 Contact Us By phone: (617) 353-5381 By e-mail: fsao@bu.edu Or by using our online form Boston University Search Directory Contact us BU Employee Wellness ©  Boston University. All rights reserved. www.bu.edu"
    }
